---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Terms of use — CareLoop';
const description =
  'CareLoop is a MIT-licensed prototype memory aid, not a clinical tool: adults only, consent of everyone recorded, no dose advice, and no warranty.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="cl-prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="u-mute">Short, honest terms for a prototype. They match how CareLoop behaves.</p>

    <div class="cl-callout warn" style="margin:var(--cl-sp-5) 0;">
      <strong>A memory aid, not a clinical tool.</strong> CareLoop repeats what a clinician said. It
      does not diagnose, treat, recommend or decide doses, and it is not a substitute for
      professional care.
    </div>

    <h2>Who may use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Adults only.</strong> CareLoop is intended for adult users and adult care plans. It
        is configured to reject content about children.</li>
      <li>You confirm you have the consent of everyone whose words or care you record before you
        paste, upload or dictate it.</li>
      <li>You keep your household PIN and linked sessions private, and you unlink any assistant you
        no longer use.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What CareLoop does and does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It only repeats the clinician&rsquo;s recorded words and grounds every item in the original
        sentence.</li>
      <li>It never gives medicine dosing advice, and it never shows doses on the voice surface.</li>
      <li>Because it works from what you record, it can be incomplete or reflect a misunderstanding
        at the visit. It is a reminder, not an authority.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="cl-callout">
      <strong>Confirm anything uncertain.</strong> If an item looks unclear, ambiguous or you are
      not sure it is right, confirm it with your clinician or pharmacist before acting. Items the
      extraction is unsure about are explicitly flagged for this reason.
    </div>

    <h2>Prototype licence and no warranty</h2>
    <p>
      CareLoop is an MIT-licensed prototype, provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and for demonstration. To the
      maximum extent permitted by law, the contributors disclaim all warranties &mdash; express or
      implied &mdash; including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement, and accept no
      liability for how you use it. Do not rely on CareLoop for medical decisions.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This is a hackathon project; these terms and the product may change without notice. Continued
      use means you accept the current terms.
    </p>

    <p class="cl-disclaimer">
      Not medical advice. In an emergency, contact your local emergency services.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
